[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Resource_5uc5c"]
script = ExtResource("41")
name = "legole0"
role = "Previous Director, Programmer & Rubicon Engine Co-creator"
description = "[center]Previously Director, Programmer, and made Rubicon alongside Annie[/center]

[center][b]I did...[/b][/center]

[center][b][u]Collector's Shop[/u][/b][/center]

• 3D Lighting Direction

• Lightmaps setup and configuration

• Point & Click System

• Screen System (Console, Kollectadex, Cartridge Bag)

• Programmed most of the Kollectadex

• Helped organize and import 3D models to the console

• Imported almost all models

• Fixed a countless amount of visual glitches

• Imported animations

• Heavy optimizing and organization

• Fixed Collector's rig multiple times

• Multiple scrapped camera controls, alongside with old lighting, and console menu




[center][b][u]Safety Lullaby[/u][/b][/center]

• 2D Lighting Direction

• Initially imported Hypno and Girlfriend

• Imported the background

• Helped fix multiple bugs and improve some visuals and performance

• Mostly worked on the previously shown iteration of Safety Lullaby, as the game had to be recoded




[center][b][u]Monochrome[/u][/b][/center]

• Added Pre-Blood Cutscene

• Adjusted Blood Cutscene, added blood characters singing

• Initially added Gold's assets, later redone

• Added multiple jumpscare animations and adjusted timings

• Small optimization to background Unowns

• Added most of the intro cutscene




[center][b][u]Chimera[/u][/b][/center]

• 3D Lighting Direction

• Lightmaps setup and configuration

• Imported House Model

• Imported Hex's Model

• Programmed Heartbeat mechanic

• Laid out events in the engine

• Imported most of Serena's animations




[b]As a director[/b] I helped come up with ideas for most of the songs, with a lot of early ideas for Monochrome and Chimera, and had a big part in how a lot of the things in the Collector's Shop worked early on, both programmatically and design wise.
I pushed for Lullaby to use Godot Engine around 2 years ago, being arguably one of the things that boosted our limits with what we can do the most, as well as providing Rubicon as the rhythm game engine of choice.
I also majorly helped put together the current team, bringing in a lot of people that ended up being in the most active of the team.



I've also worked on the website (cabinetofnovelties.com) alongside Picto, though Im mostly managing the hosting and some of the design, as I've had a very minor part in the actual coding of the site.



[left]Thanks for reading up until here. Working on this project and helping getting it back up since 2024 has been a crazy ride with a LOT of ups and downs, but overall it's been an irreplaceable experience. I've learnt so much, met such incredible people or strengthened my bonds with others, and regardless of having stepped down as a director and not having contributed as much as I'd like to, (lots of personal reasons and lots of work having to be scrapped/given out to other programmers) it has been an insane and unique opportunity and i hope you all can appreciate our efforts and enjoy what we've been pouring our hearts into.
[b]And once again, thank you from reading!!![/b]
[/left]

[img]res://assets/menus/console/credits/customemojis/thechickens.png[/img]"
socials_link = "https://x.com/legole0"
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://c3kvjgv8wyyjg"

